  "sn3.5:1.4": "For “protect themselves” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>rakkhito attā</i>) compare <i lang='pi' translate='no'>rakkhitatta</i> at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn6.13/en/sujato#2.4'>SN 6.13:2.4</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/thag2.11/en/sujato#2.4'>Thag 2.11:2.4</a>. The use of the term <i lang='pi' translate='no'>attā</i> here is conventional, not metaphysical. “Personal safety” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>ātmarakṣā</i>) is a paramount concern of kings (eg. Arthaśāstra 1.1.3, 1.21.30, 5.4.16, 7.3.24, 9.6.40, 12.2.10). ",
